# Development Environment Variables
# This file is committed to the repository for easy local development
#
# IMPORTANT: This is ONLY for local development!
# Production deployments (Render, etc.) override these with secure platform-generated values
#
# To run locally: Just clone the repo and run `python app.py` - it works immediately!

# Flask Secret Key (Development Only)
# Used for: session security, CSRF protection, and database encryption
# This key is safe to commit because:
#   1. It's only used in local development
#   2. Production platforms (Render) override with their own secure key via environment variables
#   3. Your local database is never exposed to the internet
SECRET_KEY=dev-local-ministering-interviews-key-not-for-production-use-12345678
